    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_mev_tooltip">Minimum Effective Volume — the lowest weekly hard sets where your logs still show progress. Estimated from your volume and strength trends; blended with research ranges when data is sparse.</string>
    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_mav_tooltip">Maximum Adaptive Volume — the weekly hard sets where your progress peaks. Fit from a quadratic dose-response model on your volume vs. strength trends; the vertex of the curve.</string>
    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_mrv_tooltip">Maximum Recoverable Volume — the highest weekly hard sets you recovered from while still progressing. Estimated from your training history; blended with research ranges when data is sparse.</string>
    <string name="gym_lifts_import_summary_pv_tooltip">Pareto Volume — the weekly hard sets reaching 80% of your peak progress. The point beyond which extra volume yields diminishing returns, fit from the ascending limb of your dose-response curve.</string>
